/-!
# Area `AppXIField`: the field-theoretic content of Appendix XI Prop. 1 (2)b

This is the base module of the area `AppXIField` of the Bender–Suzuki project (BS design
pass 17, Brief 4).  It contains **only definitions** (plus their elementary API); the theorems
live in `Submission/Work/AppXIField/L0/` and `Submission/Work/AppXIField/Main/`.

## The two things the area owes

* **L0** `Work.AppXIField.field_of_free_comm_action`: a finite abelian group `V` (odd order) on
  which the finite abelian group `A` acts freely outside `0` with `|V| ≤ 2|A| + 1` is the
  additive group of a finite field `K`, with `A ↪ Kˣ` acting by multiplication and a group `B`
  acting by ring automorphisms (Schur + Wedderburn; App. XI Prop. 2, first half).
* **The target** `Work.AppXIField.nearFieldFieldPropNI_of : NearFieldAppXIPropPlus →
  NearFieldFieldPropNI`: the `𝓕`-form of App. XI Prop. 1 (2)b, i.e. the near-field quotient
  `R/N` of Ch. V §3 step (2) is a finite field of cardinality `o(st)^m = |C_Q(P)| + 1` on
  which `Σ = C_W(P)` acts by automorphisms, with `Fix σ_w = {0} ∪ ι(C_{C_Q(P)}(w))`.

Both are stated in the vocabulary of `Work.ThmF.ChV3` (`CtxF`, `CQ`, `Sig`, `Ker`,
`NearFieldAppXIProp`).  The two `Prop`s below are copied **verbatim** from the pass-17 design
file `Submission/Work/_design17/ThmF17_AppXI.lean` (`namespace Design17.XI`); the duplicates in
the sibling areas `AppXIShadow`/`AppXIDickson` are definitionally equal, since the bodies are
the same term.

## The route for L0 (for the prover of `field_of_free_comm_action`)

*Freeness in orbits.*  If `a ≠ 1` then `v ↦ a • v` has no nonzero fixed point, so all orbits of
`A` on `V ∖ {0}` have size exactly `Nat.card A`; hence `|V| = 1 + k·|A|` with `1 ≤ k` and
`hbig` forces `k ≤ 2` (this also gives `|A| ≥ (|V|-1)/2`).

*Irreducibility.*  For an `A`-invariant additive subgroup `0 < W < V`: `W ∖ {0}` is a union of
orbits, whence `|W| ≥ |A| + 1`, while `|V| = [V:W]·|W| ≥ 2·|W|` (the index is `≠ 1` because
`W ≠ ⊤`).  So `|V| ≥ 2|A| + 2 > 2|A| + 1 ≥ |V|`, absurd.  In the vocabulary below: `V` is a
module over `R := actSubring A V` (a subring of `AddMonoid.End V`, with the `Module` instance
`instModuleActSubring` for which `r • v = (r : V →+ V) v`), and `IsSimpleModule R V` follows
because the `R`-submodules are exactly the `A`-invariant additive subgroups (`Subring.closure`
is generated by the `A`-action, and conversely each `actEnd A V a` preserves such a subgroup).
Note `hodd` is *not* needed: `[V : W] ≥ 2` suffices at the Irreducibility step.

*The field* `K := Module.End (actSubring A V) V = End_A V`.  It is a division ring by Schur
(`Module.End.instDivisionRing`, needs `[DecidableEq]`, available from `[Finite V]`), hence a
field by `littleWedderburn` (`[Finite V]`).  The map `ι : A →* Kˣ`, `ι a = (v ↦ a • v)`
(inverse `v ↦ a⁻¹ • v`; multiplicativity uses commutativity of `A`), is injective by `hfree`
applied to `v ≠ 0`, so `|A| ≤ |K|-1`.

*The additive isomorphism.*  Pick `v₀ ≠ 0` (from `hV`) and let `Φ : K →+ V`, `Φ k = k v₀`
(where `k` acts on `V` through the `Module (Module.End R V) V` instance).  `Φ` is injective: if
`k ≠ 0` then `k` is invertible (Schur), so `k v₀ = 0` forces `v₀ = 0`.  Its image is an additive
subgroup of size `|K| ≥ |A| + 1`, so if `Φ` were not surjective then `|V| ≥ 2|K| ≥ 2|A| + 2 >
2|A| + 1 ≥ |V|`.  Hence `Φ` is bijective and `e := Φ.symm : V ≃+ K` satisfies `e (a • v) =
(ι a) * e v` (both sides are the unique `k` with `k • v₀ = a • v`), and `e v₀ = 1`.

*The ring is generated by `ι(A)`.*  Let `S := Subring.closure (Set.range ι)`.  `S` is a finite
subring of the field `K`, so every `0 ≠ x ∈ S` has `x⁻¹ ∈ S` (multiplication by `x` is an
injective self-map of the finite set `S`), and for `u ∉ S` the map `S × S → K`, `(x,y) ↦ x + u y`
is injective, whence `|K| ≥ |S|²` if `S ≠ K`.  But `|S| ≥ |A| + 1 ≥ (|K|+1)/2` (`0 ∈ S`, and `A`
injects into `S ∖ {0}` through `ι`), so `|K| ≥ |S|² ≥ ((|K|+1)/2)²` i.e. `(|K|-1)² ≤ 0`, absurd.
Hence `S = K`: any two ring automorphisms of `K` agreeing on `ι(A)` are equal
(`Subring.closure_le` applied to the equalizer `{x | τ₁ x = τ₂ x}`), which is the last conjunct
of L0.

*The action of `B`.*  For `b : B` define `σ_b k := e (b • (k • v₀)) / e (b • v₀)` (a field
division; note `e (b • v₀) ≠ 0` since `b` is bijective and `v₀ ≠ 0`).  Then `σ_b` is additive,
`σ_b 1 = 1`, and `σ_b (ι a) = ι (φ b a)` by `hcompat` applied to `b • v₀`; multiplicativity on
`ι(A)` follows from `φ b` being a group homomorphism, and multiplicativity everywhere follows
from `S = K` by the standard induction ("if `f` is additive and multiplicative on a generating
set, then `f` is a ring homomorphism" — prove `σ f (x*y) = σ f x * σ f y` for all `x, y` in the
subring generated, by induction on `x`).  Each `σ_b` is an injective ring endomorphism of the
finite field `K`, hence a ring equivalence (`RingEquiv.ofBijective`/`RingHom` +
`Finite.injective_iff_surjective`); `σ_1 = 1` and `σ_{b b'} = σ_b ∘ σ_{b'}` (both sides are ring
homomorphisms agreeing on the generating set `ι(A)`).  A slicker equivalent description of the
same map: `σ_b k = b ∘ k ∘ b⁻¹`, which is a ring automorphism of `AddMonoid.End V` preserving
`Module.End R V` (it commutes with `A` because `b` is `φ`-semilinear); either description
proves the statement.

## The route for `nearFieldFieldPropNI_of`

See the docstrings of `Submission/Work/AppXIField/Main/`.  In short: apply `hNFp` to get
`m', R, N` with `N = Ker H Q P t`, `R ≤ C_G(P)`, `C_G(P) ≤ N_G(R) ∩ N_G(N)`, `|R| = |N|·f^{m'}`,
`|C_Q(P)| + 1 = f^{m'}` (`f = o(st)` prime) and the fixed-point-freeness clause; put
`V := Additive (↥R ⧸ N.subgroupOf R)` (commutative since `[R,R] ≤ N`), let `A = C_Q(P)` and
`B = Σ = Sig H t P` act by conjugation (`Σ ≤ C_G(P) ⊓ H` and `H ≤ N_G(Q)`, so both normalise
`C_Q(P)`), and apply L0.  The fixed points of `σ_w` are `{0} ∪ ι(C_{C_Q(P)}(w))` because
`ι` is bijective onto `Fˣ` (`|C_Q(P)| = |F| - 1`) and `σ_w (ι a) = ι (w a w⁻¹)`.
-/

